Chapter: BoundedReturnTrap

 Bounded signatures, stage B (postcondition): an out-of-range result
 traps before the return. clamp-ret's declared return is bounded 0..15
 and its body passes through the plain-Integer parameter 99, so the
 return guard traps with UD2.

 The __narrow is load-bearing and this test did not have it until
 2026-07-27, which is why it stopped compiling. CDX2051 refuses a
 bounded return whose value has an unproven range rather than inserting
 a check nobody asked for; __narrow is the request, and it traps at
 runtime exactly as its diagnostic promises.

Section: Definitions

  clamp-ret : Integer -> Integer between 0 and 15
  clamp-ret (n) = __narrow n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (clamp-ret 99))
  end
